#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:1
msgid "Release 2.7 (2022-03-07)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:3
msgid ""
"Nix will now make some helpful suggestions when you mistype something on the "
"command line. For instance, if you type `nix build nixpkgs#thunderbrd`, it "
"will suggest `thunderbird`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:7
msgid ""
"A number of \"default\" flake output attributes have been renamed. These are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:10
msgid "`defaultPackage.<system>` → `packages.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:11
msgid "`defaultApps.<system>` → `apps.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:12
msgid "`defaultTemplate` → `templates.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:13
msgid "`defaultBundler.<system>` → `bundlers.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:14
msgid "`overlay` → `overlays.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:15
msgid "`devShell.<system>` → `devShells.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:17
msgid ""
"The old flake output attributes still work, but `nix flake check` will warn "
"about them."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:20
msgid ""
"Breaking API change: `nix bundle` now supports bundlers of the form `bundler."
"<system>.<name>= derivation: another-derivation;`. This supports additional "
"functionality to inspect evaluation information during bundling. A new "
"[repository](https://github.com/NixOS/bundlers) has various bundlers "
"implemented."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:27
msgid "`nix store ping` now reports the version of the remote Nix daemon."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:29
msgid ""
"`nix flake {init,new}` now display information about which files have been "
"created."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:32
msgid ""
"Templates can now define a `welcomeText` attribute, which is printed out by "
"`nix flake {init,new} --template <template>`."
msgstr ""
